<title>NEW ZEALAND: Mercury, Utilicorp plan joint control of Power NZ.</title>
<headline>Mercury, Utilicorp plan joint control of Power NZ.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Auckland power retailer Mercury Energy and Kansas-based Utilicorp United Inc on Tuesday gave up long-running battle for control of Auckland power retailer Power New Zealand and proposed joint control.</p>
<p>In a joint statement, the pair offered minority shareholders NZ$6 per share after earlier each withdrawing takeover offers at $8 per share.</p>
</text>
